@*
    OdsInfiniteList — the card-list counterpart to OdsInlinePager (Odyssey Design System ·
    Components kit InfiniteList).

    For the expandable card pages (Accounts, Budgets), which fetch their full set (the overview /
    net-worth needs every row) and would be heavy to render all at once. It renders the first
    BatchSize cards and appends the next batch when an IntersectionObserver sentinel near the end
    scrolls into view; a centered status pill reports "X of N loaded". The only size control is the
    toolbar's "Load N at a time" batch size (an OdsPageSizeSelect the page owns). `Trailing` (e.g.
    an OdsAddRow) renders only once everything is loaded, since it would be unreachable mid-scroll.
    `RevealKey` force-loads up to a specific item (the Accounts "jump to" so a flagged card beyond
    the window still renders + scrolls into view).

    Platform note: unlike the DS prototype (which fakes a 500ms fetch + skeletons), the rows are
    already in memory here, so the append is immediate and the pill rests at "scroll for more" —
    no dishonest spinner.
*@

@typeparam TItem
@implements IAsyncDisposable
@inject IJSRuntime JS

@* The list never assembles its own loading / error / empty states — OdsListStatus owns all four
   and this component owns only the windowing, so a card page cannot render "nothing here yet"
   for a failed load without saying so. *@
<OdsListStatus Loading="Loading" Refetching="Refetching" Error="Error" OnRetry="OnRetry"
               ErrorDescription="@ErrorDescription"
               IsEmpty="@(Total == 0)" HasFilters="HasFilters" OnClearFilters="OnClearFilters"
               Noun="@Noun" EmptyIcon="@EmptyIcon" EmptyTitle="@EmptyTitle"
               EmptyDescription="@EmptyDescription" CreateAction="CreateAction" Empty="Empty"
               BarClass="@BarClass">
    @* No wrapper element — the rendered card is a direct child of the host list container so its
       `.acct-list > .acct-item` styling holds. (Card expand state lives in the host page, keyed by
       item id, so omitting @key is safe.) *@
    @foreach (var item in Items.Take(Shown))
    {
        @RenderItem(item)
    }

    @if (HasMore)
    {
        <div @ref="_sentinel" aria-hidden="true" style="height:1px"></div>
        @* The pill is a real button so the next batch is reachable by keyboard (WCAG 2.1.1), not
           only by scrolling the IntersectionObserver sentinel into view. It stays inside the
           aria-live status region, whose text updates ("X of N") as batches load. *@
        <div class="odc-infinite-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">
            <button type="button" class="odc-infinite-pill" @onclick="Grow"
                    aria-label="@($"Load more — {Shown:N0} of {Total:N0} {Noun} loaded")">
                <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:16px">expand_more</span>
                @Shown.ToString("N0") of @Total.ToString("N0") @Noun · load more
            </button>
        </div>
    }
    else if (Trailing is not null)
    {
        @Trailing
    }
</OdsListStatus>
